# GENERATED by tacctl. Edits here are overwritten, and there is no way to adopt one.
#
# The main dictionary of tacctl's FreeRADIUS instance: the unit starts the daemon with
# '-D <this directory>', which makes it read this file in place of the package's main
# dictionary. That one is included first, unchanged; no file of the package is edited.

$INCLUDE /usr/share/freeradius/dictionary

# WTI (Western Telematic Inc.) console servers and power units: the access level of a login.
# Written by tacctl from the numbers WTI publishes; not a copy of WTI's file, which also has
# attributes tacctl does not send and carries no licence statement:
#   https://ftp.wti.com/InfoCenter/rsa/dictionary/dictionary.wti
# The value names are those of the WTI user's guide (the published file has none).
VENDOR		WTI			24496
BEGIN-VENDOR	WTI
ATTRIBUTE	WTI-Super		41	integer
VALUE		WTI-Super		ViewOnly	0
VALUE		WTI-Super		User	1
VALUE		WTI-Super		SuperUser	2
VALUE		WTI-Super		Administrator	3
END-VENDOR	WTI

# tacctl's own attributes. A users entry sets them in the control list and the policy in
# tacctl-radius.conf makes the vendor attributes of a reply from them. They are numbered in
# the range FreeRADIUS reserves for site-local attributes (3000-3999), which it never puts
# into a RADIUS packet.
ATTRIBUTE	Tacctl-Priv-Lvl     	3990	integer
ATTRIBUTE	Tacctl-Juniper-Class	3991	string
ATTRIBUTE	Tacctl-WTI-Super    	3992	integer
